{"source": "The enemies of a world-map encounter on the battle map (part 9, 09d round 2, Marek 11-23: \"a battle arena per terrain - lets go for it\"): one statblock a kind, keyed as the world map's kinds are (raiders:*, bands, patrol:*, traders, creature:<name>). The raider is the Battle tab's own (Nájezdník 2); every creature's numbers are MINE, EXAMPLE, in Fallout 2's scale; hp empty = the world map's own (the kill XP's HP). mob = the Minecraft stand-in, creature = our own model (Creatures). meat_kg and hides = what a dead creature gives the party that holds the field (09d round 3: food from a hunt; a portion is 0.5 kg; the Hunter perk doubles both) [mine, EXAMPLE]. The players' kit and a death in it are still the battle demo's. Round 5 (09d, Marek 11-24: \"we need more enemies with bows and melee weapons\"): a raider group draws each figure's kit (Arena.kitFor): the pistol raider, the archer (a bow of weapons.json) or the melee raider (a melee weapon of it); reserve = the rounds or arrows carried besides the loaded ones (they hoard them; none left = the knife); parts = a creature's special parts for the field (the skill and level they need, fragile = ruined unless the butcher puts them first) [mine, EXAMPLE].", "rows": [
